# Local secrets/configuration (including nested app environment files).
#
# ENG-019: nothing matching `.env*` is tracked any more, not even a template.
# Agent sandboxes deny writes to every such path — correctly, since that is
# where secrets live — but the rule matched the tracked `.env.example` template
# too, so a sandboxed agent could not check the repository out at all. It failed
# on `error: unable to create file .env.example: Operation not permitted` before
# running a single test. The template now lives at `env.example`, with no
# leading dot, and the exceptions below are gone: a `.env*` path in this
# repository is a secret, without exception, which is a simpler rule anyway.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets/

# Dependencies and generated build/test output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Regenerated by `next typegen`; its contents differ between dev and build.
next-env.d.ts
.turbo/
.vercel/

# Logs, local data, recordings and databases
*.log
/recordings/
uploads/
local-data/
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.webm
*.ogg
*.flac
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Local editor/OS and agent overrides
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
CLAUDE.local.md

# Python controller artifacts and local loop evidence
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.agent-runs/
